{
  "id": "pi-back-calculation-sixth-control",
  "name": "PI control with actuator saturation and back-calculation",
  "description": "Original normalized first-order plant with PI controller and finite-gain back-calculation anti-windup. Integral_Output is the signed integral contribution to actuator command; it is not accumulated error and can be negative. Command=Proportional_Gain*(Setpoint-Output)+Integral_Output; actual actuator is explicitly bounded. Integral derivative adds Integral_Gain*error and Tracking_Rate*(Actuator-Command). Time seconds; output, reference, actuator and integral contribution normalized dimensionless. Positive Plant_Time; nonnegative plant gain, proportional/integral/tracking gains; Actuator_Min < Actuator_Max. Original illustrative defaults, no delay, derivative control, rate limit, noise, feedforward or tuning/stability guarantee. Tracking_Rate=0 disables anti-windup. Numerical steps must resolve plant and tracking time scales.",
  "category": "engineering",
  "source": "https://cse.lab.imtlucca.it/~bemporad/teaching/controllodigitale/pdf/Astrom-ACC89.pdf",
  "reference": "Astrom,K.J. and Rundqwist,L.(1989), Integrator Windup and How to Avoid It, American Control Conference pp1693-1698, doi:10.23919/ACC.1989.4790464, printed p1694 Figure2. Original normalized plant/defaults; PI specialization of back-calculation, no paper text/code/figures redistributed.",
